., Gonzalez A., Ackermann G.L., Cerrano C., Astudillo-Garcia C., Easson C., Sipkema D., Liu F., et al. The sponge microbiome project. GigaScience. 2017;6:gix077. doi: 10.1093/gigascience/gix077.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1093/gigascience/gix077</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5632291</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">29020741</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Pita L., Rix L., Slaby B.M., Franke A., Hentschel U. The sponge holobiont in a changing ocean: From microbes to ecosystems. Microbiome. 2018;6:46. doi: 10.1186/s40168-018-0428-1.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1186/s40168-018-0428-1</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5845141</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">29523192</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Hentschel U., Piel J., Degnan S.M., Taylor M.W. Genomic insights into the marine sponge microbiome. Nat. Rev. Microbiol. 2012;10:641&#x2013;654. doi: 10.1038/nrmicro2839.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/nrmicro2839</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">22842661</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Zhang H., Wang M., Wang H., Chen H., Cao L., Zhong Z., Lian C., Zhou L., Li C. Metagenome sequencing and 768 microbial genomes from cold seep in South China Sea. Sci. Data. 2022;9:480. doi: 10.1038/s41597-022-01586-x.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/s41597-022-01586-x</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC9357000</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">35933411</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Wang Y., Gong L., Gao Z., Wang Y., Zhao F., Fu L., Li X. Host-specific bacterial communities associated with six cold-seep sponge species in the South China Sea. Front. Mar. Sci. 2023;10:1243952.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Wang Y., Gong L., Dong D., Li X. Metagenomic binning reveals community and functional characteristics of sulfur- and methane-oxidizing b